      "problem": "What number can be added to $-28$ to get a sum of $0?$",
      "worked_solution": "The number that can be added to $-28$ to give $0$ is the additive inverse of $-28.$\n\nTo find the additive inverse of the number $-28,$ we change its sign by placing a minus symbol $({\\color{red}{-}})$ in front of it. So, we obtain \n\n$$\n{\\color{red}{-}}\\,(-28) = 28.\n$$\n\nTo check our work, we add the inverse to the original number. If we're correct, we should get zero.\n\n$$\n(-28)+28 = -28+28= 0 \\quad {\\color{green}\\checkmark}\n$$",
